<h1 id="c:cob-hyp" class="tex-chapter"><span data-tag="00AB">15</span> Cobordism hypothesis</h1>

<p>
In this chapter, we give a definition of fully extended TQFT in any dimension, using the language of $(\infty ,n)$ categories, and present one of the key results of this theory, the cobordism hypothesis, which classifies such $n$-dimensional extended theories in terms of <em>fully dualizable</em> objects. 
</p>
<p>
Our exposition follows the foundational paper <span class="cite">[<a href="/bibliography/lurie-cobordism">Lur2009a</a>]</span> by Jacob Lurie; a short exposition can also be found in <span class="cite">[<a href="/bibliography/freed-cobordism">Fre2013</a>]</span>. 
</p>
